# The build context is the REPO ROOT, so BuildKit reads this file.
#
# Two things here are load-bearing in a way they were not when the context was
# a subdirectory:
#
#   .env / .env.*  the real secrets file now sits inside the context
#   .git           the whole history now sits inside the context
#
# And `lab` is what keeps 761 MB of scrape evidence out of the daemon. Both
# Dockerfiles end their build stage with `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded
# here is transferred and then baked into a layer.
#
# Sanity check after editing this file:
#   docker build -f apps/api/Dockerfile -t bw-api:test . 2>&1 | grep "transferring context"
# Single-digit MB is right. Hundreds means something below stopped matching.

# Secrets and history -- keep these first.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
.githooks

# Lab notebooks: 761 MB on disk, plus a tracked 16.6 MB catalogue.db.
lab

# Docs and tooling that no image needs -- except the collector manifest,
# which the API reads at runtime for provisioning.
docs
!docs/collector-manifest.json
.claude
.playwright-mcp
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__

# Build output and dependency trees. pnpm's symlink farm holds absolute paths
# into /Users/... that do not exist in the container, and copying it produces
# an ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND deep in a build with no obvious cause.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

**/*.md
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
